# XSH mq_getattr()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Message passing option (MSG). EBADF is a may-fail error here and is not
# tested.

assertion  XSH.mq_getattr.001
anchor     functions/mq_getattr.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/mq_getattr.html#RETURN VALUE
class      conditional
when       MSG
since      2001
says       mq_getattr() on a fresh queue created with 4 and 64 and opened
           without O_NONBLOCK returns 0 with mq_maxmsg 4, mq_msgsize 64,
           mq_curmsgs 0 and no O_NONBLOCK in mq_flags.
test       t/001-fresh.c

assertion  XSH.mq_getattr.002
anchor     functions/mq_getattr.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       MSG
since      2001
says       mq_curmsgs is the number of messages on the queue: 0, then 3 after
           three sends (also seen through a write-only descriptor), then 2
           after a receive.
test       t/002-curmsgs.c

assertion  XSH.mq_getattr.003
anchor     functions/mq_getattr.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       MSG
since      2001
says       mq_flags is that of the open description: a description opened
           with O_NONBLOCK shows it, another one of the same queue does not,
           and both report the same mq_maxmsg and mq_msgsize.
test       t/003-flags-per-description.c
